        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued July 26 at 2:49PM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "Water levels are expected to rise to 1 to 1.5 feet above the\nnormal high tide line around the Kotzebue Sound and Chukchi Sea\nCoast around late Sunday, peaking overnight and diminishing\nrapidly on Monday morning due to gusty northwesterly winds\nbetween 25 & 35 mph behind the cold front that has moved through.",
