        "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued July 26 at 2:42PM AKDT by NWS Fairbanks AK",
        "description": "An Arctic cold front is has been moving southeast from the\nChukchi Sea today. Total snow accumulations of 2-6\" is possible\nin the Brooks Range with less than an inch expected for most of\nthe Eastern Arctic Coast. Periods of freezing drizzle are possible\nas the snow diminishes this afternoon and evening.",
        "severity": "Moderate",
        "certainty": "Observed",
